>> title: Baked Turkey Wings, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: turkey, gravy, southern, braise, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: baked-turkey-wings
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: turkey wings, smothered turkey wings, turkey necks, baked turkey wings and gravy, slow cooker turkey wings, crockpot smothered turkey wings
>> pairs-with: onion-gravy, candied-yams, cornbread-dressing, collard-greens
>> servings: 4
>> time: 7 hr
>> slack: forgiving — a turkey wing is collagen and skin, and at six hours or eight it either stays on the bone or falls off it and both are dinner; the skin is the part with no room, and it was never going to stay crisp under a lid
>> step.2: season, under the skin too
>> step.3: roast uncovered 425°F 40 min
>> step.4: braise on low, 6 hr
>> step.5: thicken on high, lid off

Written for low, six hours, and the colour happens in the oven first — this is the only file on the shelf that browns somewhere other than a skillet, because a wing is an awkward shape to turn in a pan and a sheet tray does all four at once. Do not skip it. Straight into the crock they steam, and a steamed turkey wing comes out grey. Be honest about what the machine then does to that skin: it softens it. What you keep is the colour and the roasted flavour in the gravy, not a crackling wing. The gravy comes down from four cups to two and a half, because nothing evaporates.

Season @turkey wings{4%lb}(1.8 kg; split at the joints) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{2%tsp}, @poultry seasoning{1%tsp}, working some of it under the skin.

Roast @&(~1)seasoned wings{} on a bed of @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced) in an #oven{} at 425°F (220°C) for ~roast{40%min}, until the skin has taken real colour.

Slow cook @&(~1)coloured wings{} with @onion gravy{2 1/2%cup}(590 mL) in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{6%hr}, lid on, the wings overlapped rather than stacked.

Thicken @&(~1)smothered wings{} on high with the lid off, stirring in @cornstarch{1%Tbs}(8 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) for ~thicken{20%min}, with the wings lifted out. Carve nothing — the wing goes to the plate whole with the gravy over it.
